┃  Prompting                                                                                                                                   ┃
┃    enter                 send prompt                                                                                                         ┃
┃    shift+enter           insert newline (also ctrl+j, ctrl+enter, alt+enter)                                                                 ┃
┃    /                     open available commands, including workspace commands when enabled                                                  ┃
┃    ? or /help            open this help; the shortcut works when the prompt is empty                                                         ┃
┃    @                     attach a file; supported images and audio are sent as media, other files as text                                    ┃
┃    ctrl+v                paste a clipboard image, or paste text when image attachments are unavailable                                       ┃
┃    ctrl+u                clear the current draft                                                                                             ┃
┃    esc, release, esc     clear the current idle draft within 500ms; the first press makes no visible change                                  ┃
┃                          also clears attachments, large pasted text, and pending media; requires a terminal with enhanced key-event support  ┃
┃                          fixed shortcut; repeats do not count, and other views handle esc first                                              ┃
┃                          use the remappable Clear prompt action (ctrl+u) on any terminal                                                     ┃
┃  lines 1–14 of 68 · esc or ? close · ↑/↓ scroll · pgup/pgdn page · home/end jump                                                             ┃
